---
import Site from "../layouts/Site.astro";
import CTA from "../components/CTA.astro";
import AuditClose from "../components/AuditClose.astro";
---

<Site
  page="approach"
  title="Our Approach | Anchorline Systems"
  description="We start with where growth is breaking down. Then we connect strategy, intelligence, technology, and hands-on execution around what your organization needs."
>
  <section class="container r-inner-hero r-split">
    <div class="r-editorial">
      <p class="eyebrow">OUR APPROACH</p><h1>
        A better way<br />to get growth working.
      </h1><p class="r-lede">
        We don’t start with tools. We start with where growth is actually
        breaking down.
      </p><p>
        Your offer, your customers, your people, and the way work moves through
        the organization tell us more than a list of software ever could.
      </p><div class="r-actions"><CTA location="approach-hero" /></div>
    </div>
    <div class="r-priority-visual" data-reveal>
      <article class="r-priority-paper">
        <span class="mono">GROWTH PRIORITIES / EXAMPLE FORMAT</span><h3>
          Understand the problem.<br />Find the right next move.
        </h3><ol>
          <li>
            <span>01</span><div>
              <strong>See the whole picture</strong><p>
                Acquisition, visibility, conversion, and follow-up.
              </p>
            </div>
          </li><li>
            <span>02</span><div>
              <strong>Locate the disconnect</strong><p>
                Where does opportunity lose momentum?
              </p>
            </div>
          </li><li>
            <span>03</span><div>
              <strong>Prioritize what matters</strong><p>
                A practical configuration and a clear next step.
              </p>
            </div>
          </li>
        </ol><p class="r-priority-foot">
          Illustrative framework, not a client assessment.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container r-approach-principles">
    <div>
      <span class="mono">01 / UNDERSTAND</span><h3>
        Context before<br />a recommendation.
      </h3><p>
        Look at how the organization actually works. Keep what is effective.
        Identify the gaps that matter to the intended outcome.
      </p>
    </div><div>
      <span class="mono">02 / CONNECT</span><h3>
        A system.<br />Not a shopping list.
      </h3><p>
        Choose the capabilities, responsibilities, and infrastructure that need
        to work together. Give every part a purpose.
      </p>
    </div><div>
      <span class="mono">03 / FOLLOW THROUGH</span><h3>
        Execution with<br />a feedback loop.
      </h3><p>
        Build the agreed pieces, review what happens, and use the evidence to
        improve the next decision.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="r-section container r-split">
    <div class="r-editorial">
      <p class="eyebrow">STRATEGY MEETS THE OPERATING REALITY</p><h2>
        Good thinking matters.<br />What happens next<br />matters just as much.
      </h2>
    </div><div class="editorial-copy">
      <p class="large-copy">
        The recommendation is the beginning of the work—not the end of it.
      </p><p>
        An engagement defines what Anchorline builds, what it operates, what
        your team owns, and how progress is reviewed. That can mean connecting a
        better website to the sales path, making buyer intelligence useful to a
        conversation, or giving local inquiries a dependable follow-up.
      </p><p>
        AI and automation can help the work move faster. They don’t replace
        judgment, ownership, or knowing what the organization is trying to
        accomplish.
      </p><a class="text-link" href="/growth-engine/"
        >Explore the Growth Engine <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section process-section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">FROM CLARITY TO EXECUTION</p><h2>
        A practical way forward.
      </h2><ol class="engagement-steps">
        <li>
          <span class="mono">01</span><h3>Audit</h3><p>
            Identify three prioritized opportunities, supporting observations, a
            recommended configuration, and a next step.
          </p>
        </li><li>
          <span class="mono">02</span><h3>Agree</h3><p>
            Define the scope, responsibilities, success measures, and work that
            matters first.
          </p>
        </li><li>
          <span class="mono">03</span><h3>Build</h3><p>
            Connect the assets, processes, and infrastructure needed to support
            the agreed outcome.
          </p>
        </li><li>
          <span class="mono">04</span><h3>Improve</h3><p>
            Review the signals, learn from execution, and refine the system as
            evidence develops.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>
  <AuditClose title="Start with where growth is breaking down." />
</Site>
